  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "37131302",
      "title": "Accepting & Passing Functions as Values",
      "lectureOrder": 60,
      "videoOrder": 57,
      "sourceHash": "f63448cbd2dce75ee66584b31153812ea80671c022f7d65d89c06d9f115a64cf",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.13,
          "end": 4.98,
          "en": "So what's this lifting state up concept",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.98,
          "end": 6.12,
          "en": "all about?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.12,
          "end": 9.57,
          "en": "Well, at the moment in our application we have the problem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.57,
          "end": 12.21,
          "en": "that we have the StartScreen, which welcomes the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.21,
          "end": 15.36,
          "en": "and provides the Start Quiz button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.36,
          "end": 17.88,
          "en": "But we then also have the QuestionsScreen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.88,
          "end": 21.72,
          "en": "to which we wanna navigate when that button is pressed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.72,
          "end": 24.48,
          "en": "So the problem that we have here is that the button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.48,
          "end": 28.59,
          "en": "that should trigger the state change is in one widget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.59,
          "end": 32.37,
          "en": "and the widget that should be affected by the state change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.37,
          "end": 34.14,
          "en": "is another widget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.14,
          "end": 37.98,
          "en": "So we have kind of two widgets that need to work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.98,
          "end": 41.043,
          "en": "with the same state or that depend on the same state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.03,
          "end": 44.91,
          "en": "And the solution here is to lift the state up,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.91,
          "end": 47.94,
          "en": "which is why we already created that quiz widget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.94,
          "end": 50.88,
          "en": "If we manage our state in that quiz widget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.88,
          "end": 52.62,
          "en": "and we then also have the function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.62,
          "end": 54.57,
          "en": "for manipulating the state in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.57,
          "end": 58.56,
          "en": "we can conveniently move between these two different widgets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.56,
          "end": 61.05,
          "en": "by rendering content conditionally.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.05,
          "end": 62.97,
          "en": "And that's of course what we're already doing here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 62.97,
          "end": 65.97,
          "en": "We do already manage and update some state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 65.97,
          "end": 68.13,
          "en": "in this quiz widget in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 68.13,
          "end": 72.06,
          "en": "in the state class that is connected to this quiz widget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 72.06,
          "end": 75.53999999999999,
          "en": "And we are rendering the content conditionally already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 75.53999999999999,
          "end": 78.42,
          "en": "So we basically already lifted the state up,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 78.42,
          "end": 82.56,
          "en": "but we haven't connected this switchScreen function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 82.56,
          "end": 85.2,
          "en": "to the screen that contains the button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 85.2,
          "end": 89.03999999999999,
          "en": "that should trigger this function or this method here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 89.03999999999999,
          "end": 90.72,
          "en": "And that is another important,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.72,
          "end": 93.99000000000001,
          "en": "and therefore, at the moment, missing aspect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 93.99000000000001,
          "end": 97.44,
          "en": "of this lifting the state up concept.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 97.44,
          "end": 100.14,
          "en": "It's not enough to just manage the state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 100.14,
          "end": 103.59,
          "en": "in some shared parent widget, Which quiz here is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 103.59,
          "end": 104.7,
          "en": "it's the parent widget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 104.7,
          "end": 107.75999999999999,
          "en": "of both StartScreen and QuestionsScreen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 107.75999999999999,
          "end": 110.55,
          "en": "but it's not enough to just manage the state here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 110.55,
          "end": 114.33,
          "en": "but instead you also must make sure that the child widget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 114.33,
          "end": 116.72999999999999,
          "en": "that should initiate the state change,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 116.72999999999999,
          "end": 119.16,
          "en": "in this case, the StartScreen widget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 119.16,
          "end": 122.55,
          "en": "gets access to the state changing function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 122.55,
          "end": 124.59,
          "en": "defined in this parent widget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 124.59,
          "end": 127.98,
          "en": "So in this case, StartScreen needs to get access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 127.98,
          "end": 130.11,
          "en": "to this switchScreen function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 130.11,
          "end": 132.243,
          "en": "And how do we now do that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 133.14,
          "end": 136.82999999999998,
          "en": "Well, you might remember that in the previous course section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 136.82999999999998,
          "end": 139.62,
          "en": "I did explain that functions in Dart",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 139.62,
          "end": 142.82999999999998,
          "en": "are also just regular values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 142.82999999999998,
          "end": 144.48,
          "en": "There we also had a button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 144.48,
          "end": 146.46,
          "en": "that should trigger some function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 146.46,
          "end": 149.1,
          "en": "and in that case back then it was a function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 149.1,
          "end": 151.38,
          "en": "a method to find in the same file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 151.38,
          "end": 152.85,
          "en": "but still it was a method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 152.85,
          "end": 155.25,
          "en": "that should be triggered when a button was pressed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 155.25,
          "end": 159.66,
          "en": "And to do, that we passed a pointer at that function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 159.66,
          "end": 162.18,
          "en": "So we used the function name in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 162.18,
          "end": 164.88,
          "en": "as a value to that button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 164.88,
          "end": 168.21,
          "en": "and internally that button would then call that function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 168.21,
          "end": 170.07,
          "en": "when the button was pressed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 170.07,
          "end": 173.57999999999998,
          "en": "And we can do the same here with our own custom widget.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 173.57999999999998,
          "end": 178.57999999999998,
          "en": "We can pass a pointer at switchScreen to StartScreen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 178.8,
          "end": 181.71,
          "en": "So simply by using the name of that method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 181.71,
          "end": 183.603,
          "en": "switchScreen, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 184.71,
          "end": 187.41,
          "en": "So you don't add parentheses here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 187.41,
          "end": 189.78,
          "en": "because that would execute this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 189.78,
          "end": 191.97,
          "en": "when this line of code here is executed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 191.97,
          "end": 193.8,
          "en": "and that would be too early.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 193.8,
          "end": 195.39,
          "en": "Instead you just use the name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 195.39,
          "end": 197.13,
          "en": "of the function or method here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 197.13,
          "end": 200.64,
          "en": "and that in the end, under the hood, passes a pointer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 200.64,
          "end": 204.57,
          "en": "to that function as a value to StartScreen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 204.57,
          "end": 207.27,
          "en": "And inside of that StartScreen widget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 207.27,
          "end": 212.19,
          "en": "you can then use that function to call it whenever you want,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 212.19,
          "end": 214.59,
          "en": "for example, when some timer expired",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 214.59,
          "end": 217.413,
          "en": "or when this button down there was pressed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 218.28,
          "end": 220.17000000000002,
          "en": "Now, at the moment, this doesn't work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 220.17000000000002,
          "end": 223.47,
          "en": "because we're basically passing in too many arguments",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 223.47,
          "end": 227.49,
          "en": "to StartScreen because I'm passing in one argument here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 227.49,
          "end": 230.13,
          "en": "The pointer at the switchScreen function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 230.13,
          "end": 232.59,
          "en": "but StartScreen at the moment doesn't want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 232.59,
          "end": 234.48,
          "en": "any positional arguments.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 234.48,
          "end": 237.75,
          "en": "It just has this one named argument here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 237.75,
          "end": 239.49,
          "en": "Now, that can be changed though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 239.49,
          "end": 242.88,
          "en": "We can add a positional argument to StartScreen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 242.88,
          "end": 244.65,
          "en": "and we could also add a named argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 244.65,
          "end": 246.96,
          "en": "but here I'll go for a positional argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 246.96,
          "end": 249.777,
          "en": "and this argument could be called startQuiz.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 250.92,
          "end": 252.663,
          "en": "The name is totally up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 253.56,
          "end": 256.5,
          "en": "But now we're accepting this positional argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 256.5,
          "end": 258.96,
          "en": "and we should also define the type of this argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 258.96,
          "end": 261.36,
          "en": "by adding it in front of the argument name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 261.36,
          "end": 264.84,
          "en": "And here, the type is Function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 264.84,
          "end": 267.33,
          "en": "which is a special type built into Dart.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 267.33,
          "end": 270.36,
          "en": "To be precise, it's a void function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 270.36,
          "end": 273.09000000000003,
          "en": "and you should now also add parentheses here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 273.09000000000003,
          "end": 277.29,
          "en": "which simply means that startQuiz should be a function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 277.29,
          "end": 279.96,
          "en": "and function is a type built into Dart.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 279.96,
          "end": 283.62,
          "en": "So it should be a function that takes no arguments,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 283.62,
          "end": 287.61,
          "en": "because indeed, switchScreen does not take any arguments.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 287.61,
          "end": 289.68,
          "en": "So as a value for startQuiz,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 289.68,
          "end": 292.05,
          "en": "we want to get a pointer and a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 292.05,
          "end": 293.61,
          "en": "that takes no arguments",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 293.61,
          "end": 296.76,
          "en": "and that also doesn't return a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 296.76,
          "end": 300.03,
          "en": "And that's exactly what switchScreen does.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 300.03,
          "end": 302.73,
          "en": "It is a function that takes no arguments",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 302.73,
          "end": 304.86,
          "en": "and returns nothing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 304.86,
          "end": 307.74,
          "en": "And with that we're passing a pointer at this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 307.74,
          "end": 310.17,
          "en": "as a value to StartScreen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 310.17,
          "end": 313.68,
          "en": "So now we can call this function from inside StartScreen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 313.68,
          "end": 316.56,
          "en": "by simply executing startQuiz like a function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 316.56,
          "end": 319.02,
          "en": "because it is a function basically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 319.02,
          "end": 320.91,
          "en": "startQuiz is an argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 320.91,
          "end": 323.61,
          "en": "that contains a function as a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 323.61,
          "end": 325.62,
          "en": "That's what we set up here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 325.62,
          "end": 327.51,
          "en": "And I'm spending a lot of time on this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 327.51,
          "end": 330.48,
          "en": "because this can be a super confusing concept,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 330.48,
          "end": 334.11,
          "en": "but in the end, it's all about a standard Dart feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 334.11,
          "end": 337.35,
          "en": "You are able to use functions as values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 337.35,
          "end": 341.49,
          "en": "and therefore to also pass them as values to other functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 341.49,
          "end": 344.79,
          "en": "or to constructive functions as we're doing it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 344.79,
          "end": 346.56,
          "en": "But with that alone, we're not done.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 346.56,
          "end": 348.39,
          "en": "We're accepting this argument here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 348.39,
          "end": 351.69,
          "en": "But as you also learned in the previous course section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 351.69,
          "end": 353.07,
          "en": "this alone is not enough,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 353.07,
          "end": 355.08,
          "en": "because the arguments you accept here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 355.08,
          "end": 357.03,
          "en": "in your constructor function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 357.03,
          "end": 360.69,
          "en": "can, for example, not be used in your build method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 360.69,
          "end": 364.56,
          "en": "So we can't use it down there where we would want to use it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 364.56,
          "end": 366.42,
          "en": "because that's where our button is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 366.42,
          "end": 369.69,
          "en": "to which this function should be connected in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 369.69,
          "end": 373.02,
          "en": "What we should therefore do is we should add a new variable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 373.02,
          "end": 376.83,
          "en": "or even better, a final variable here to StartScreen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 376.83,
          "end": 378.84,
          "en": "because we'll only set this once",
          "zh": ""
        },
